course: dictionary
lesson: 11410
title: Words that build up over time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Accrued is a formal word. It means built up or collected little by little over time. «Over ten years, the money in Priya's savings account accrued interest.» Each year a little more interest was added, so the total grew slowly. In everyday talk you could say "built up" or "added up".
explain: Accrued also has a money meaning: owed or earned but not yet paid. «Sam had three days of accrued holiday left at work.» Sam has already earned those holiday days, but he has not taken them yet. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try "built up" in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Accrued is the past form of the verb accrue. So you may also see «The interest accrues every month» and «The interest is accruing now.» The idea is the same: something gathers slowly, a bit at a time.
fact: Accrued means built up or collected little by little over time.
fact: Accrued interest means interest that has added up on money in an account.
fact: Accrued holiday means holiday time that has been earned but not yet taken.
fact: Accrue is the base verb, and accrued is its past form.
fact: A good check: swap in "built up" or "added up". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «Over the years, the small coins in the jar accrued into a large pile of money.» What does accrued mean here? | Counted and emptied quickly | Stolen from the jar | Thrown away all at once | *Built up little by little
exercise: «Mia's bank paid her the accrued interest at the end of the year.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to accrued interest? | *Interest that has added up | Interest given by a friend | A bank card | Interest that was lost
exercise: «Ben still has five days of accrued holiday, earned but not yet taken.» What does accrued suggest? | Paid in full today | Lost for ever | Given away to a friend | *Earned, but not yet used
test: «The dust had accrued on the old books on the shelf.» What does accrued mean? | Moved to a new room | Cleaned and polished | *Gathered slowly over time | Thrown away at once
test: «Dad said the interest accrues every month, so the money grows.» Which word means the same as accrues? | Shrinks | Vanishes | *Builds up | Forgets
exam: «The company owed workers money for overtime that had accrued but was not yet paid.» What does accrued mean here? | Paid straight away | *Earned, but not yet paid | Sent back | Lost
